1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,000
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:06,070
Characters, actions, places, occupations, and events in this series

3
00:00:06,110 --> 00:00:08,750
are fictional and created for entertainment purposes only.

4
00:00:08,790 --> 00:00:13,280
They are not intended to urge or promote any behavior in the series.

5
00:00:13,320 --> 00:00:15,720
Viewer discretion is advised.

6
00:00:15,930 --> 00:00:17,300
We met before?

7
00:00:17,550 --> 00:00:19,300
It happened ten years ago.

8
00:00:19,420 --> 00:00:20,640
It’s not surprising that you forgot it.

9
00:00:20,870 --> 00:00:22,030
But you remember me.

10
00:00:22,070 --> 00:00:23,300
You’ve never forgotten me.

11
00:00:23,620 --> 00:00:25,800
Key, will you be my girlfriend?

12
00:00:26,730 --> 00:00:28,080
You got a tattoo?

13
00:00:28,580 --> 00:00:29,600
It’s pretty.

14
00:00:30,070 --> 00:00:30,900
I like it.

15
00:00:31,030 --> 00:00:32,320
It’s really over.

16
00:00:32,380 --> 00:00:33,570
From now on,

17
00:00:33,880 --> 00:00:35,330
you don’t need to worry anymore.

18
00:00:44,840 --> 00:00:45,600
Key.

19
00:00:47,670 --> 00:00:48,550
Wait.

20
00:01:11,830 --> 00:01:12,600
Mom.

21
00:01:16,410 --> 00:01:17,500
How could you do this?

22
00:01:17,760 --> 00:01:19,000
You are ruining our reputation.

23
00:01:19,690 --> 00:01:20,700
What did I do?

24
00:01:20,910 --> 00:01:22,300
How dare you talk back to me?

25
00:01:22,610 --> 00:01:23,600
It’s true.

26
00:01:23,810 --> 00:01:25,400
What did I do wrong?

27
00:01:27,039 --> 00:01:28,300
Why did you get a tattoo?

28
00:01:29,470 --> 00:01:31,050
Do you think this is appropriate?

29
00:01:31,210 --> 00:01:32,280
It’s just a tattoo.

30
00:01:32,320 --> 00:01:33,850
It doesn’t define my worth, Mom.

31
00:01:33,970 --> 00:01:35,570
-Chan. -Excuse me.

32
00:01:43,820 --> 00:01:45,150
Even though she’s your daughter,

33
00:01:46,140 --> 00:01:47,800
you shouldn’t use violence with her.

34
00:01:56,250 --> 00:01:57,300
It was you, wasn’t it?

35
00:01:58,690 --> 00:02:01,190
You interrupted and cut the meeting short the other day.

36
00:02:05,430 --> 00:02:07,550
Yes, it was me.

37
00:02:07,590 --> 00:02:08,830
Who do you think you are?

38
00:02:09,229 --> 00:02:12,400
How dare you meddle in the work of my hotel?

39
00:02:14,740 --> 00:02:17,280
Do you want to show off that you’re my daughter’s sugar baby?

40
00:02:31,250 --> 00:02:35,970
I’m sorry for meddling in Chan’s work.

41
00:02:37,960 --> 00:02:39,500
I’ll be more careful next time.

42
00:02:42,280 --> 00:02:44,000
But I’m not Chan’s sugar baby.

43
00:02:46,000 --> 00:02:48,600
Chan and I are dating.

44
00:02:56,240 --> 00:02:57,500
You are an outsider.

45
00:02:58,340 --> 00:02:59,800
Get out of this room.

46
00:03:00,560 --> 00:03:01,740
I’m going to talk to my daughter.

47
00:03:01,780 --> 00:03:02,650
No.

48
00:03:05,340 --> 00:03:06,800
She’s not going anywhere.

49
00:03:10,490 --> 00:03:12,050
Why are you acting like this?

50
00:03:12,190 --> 00:03:13,930
I’ve never taught you to behave like this.

51
00:03:14,540 --> 00:03:15,900
Why have you changed?

52
00:03:16,670 --> 00:03:18,100
I haven’t changed, Mom.

53
00:03:19,430 --> 00:03:21,050
I’m just not afraid to be myself.

54
00:03:21,900 --> 00:03:24,480
I just chose to do what is best for me.

55
00:03:24,520 --> 00:03:25,680
Best to you? How?

56
00:03:26,510 --> 00:03:27,900
Tell me how?

57
00:03:30,920 --> 00:03:32,100
Mom, please leave.

58
00:03:33,480 --> 00:03:34,700
Are you telling me to leave?

59
00:03:37,800 --> 00:03:39,170
What’s wrong with you, Chan?

60
00:03:40,710 --> 00:03:43,230
-I just don’t want us to fight. -Then tell her to leave.

61
00:03:45,720 --> 00:03:48,600
Are you taking sides with an outsider instead of your family?

62
00:03:51,060 --> 00:03:55,100
Soon, she will become a part of our family.

63
00:04:02,650 --> 00:04:03,500
No.

64
00:04:05,600 --> 00:04:07,480
This girl is not good enough for you.

65
00:04:07,860 --> 00:04:10,600
She’s not good enough for anyone in our family.

66
00:04:12,580 --> 00:04:16,959
Can you let me decide who is good enough for me?

67
00:04:19,399 --> 00:04:20,700
Mom, please leave.

68
00:04:21,269 --> 00:04:22,900
I don’t want to fight with you anymore.

69
00:04:24,010 --> 00:04:24,800
Chan.

70
00:04:29,750 --> 00:04:30,900
Mom.

71
00:04:33,950 --> 00:04:35,300
Key, are you okay?

72
00:04:37,570 --> 00:04:38,700
I’ll handle it.

73
00:04:39,970 --> 00:04:42,600
Come on, Mom. Let’s go home.

74
00:04:44,090 --> 00:04:45,430
Please, I’m begging you.

75
00:04:45,970 --> 00:04:47,100
Let’s go home.

76
00:04:50,690 --> 00:04:51,600
Mom.

77
00:06:53,830 --> 00:06:54,650
Yes.

78
00:06:56,500 --> 00:06:57,200
Sun.

79
00:06:57,730 --> 00:06:58,340
Yes?

80
00:06:58,380 --> 00:06:59,800
I need to talk to you.

81
00:07:00,570 --> 00:07:01,500
What is it?

82
00:07:03,150 --> 00:07:06,100
I can’t let your sister ruin our family’s reputation.

83
00:07:06,510 --> 00:07:09,900
You need to help me and talk some sense into her.

84
00:07:13,360 --> 00:07:15,400
How could I do that?

85
00:07:16,780 --> 00:07:20,700
To be honest, Key seems like a nice girl.

86
00:07:21,370 --> 00:07:23,000
She came from a well-known family.

87
00:07:24,540 --> 00:07:26,490
But her mom is the second wife.

88
00:07:27,740 --> 00:07:31,210
You don’t know how scandalous her mom was.

89
00:07:31,870 --> 00:07:33,680
She had a long list of bad behaviors.

90
00:07:35,400 --> 00:07:39,100
I think her daughter is not much different from her.

91
00:07:43,220 --> 00:07:45,800
They are two different people.

92
00:07:46,090 --> 00:07:48,340
We shouldn’t judge them.

93
00:07:48,380 --> 00:07:49,490
Of course, we can.

94
00:07:49,909 --> 00:07:53,080
The apple doesn’t fall far from the tree.

95
00:07:53,120 --> 00:07:54,850
Because children learn from their parents.

96
00:07:55,770 --> 00:07:58,900
Mom, I’m her twin sister.

97
00:07:59,130 --> 00:08:02,100
I can tell that she is serious about her.

98
00:08:03,060 --> 00:08:04,100
One more thing:

99
00:08:04,490 --> 00:08:06,720
it doesn’t matter what kind of person Key is.

100
00:08:07,070 --> 00:08:10,920
I think Chan has thought it through before dating Key.

101
00:08:11,770 --> 00:08:13,830
If that were the case, I wouldn’t have been worried.

102
00:08:14,370 --> 00:08:16,920
But she is serious about her. She’s even thinking about marrying her.

103
00:08:16,960 --> 00:08:18,360
I can’t let it happen.

104
00:08:21,000 --> 00:08:23,000
I have to stop this.

105
00:08:28,020 --> 00:08:29,200
Mom.

106
00:08:29,910 --> 00:08:33,400
Chan has never disobeyed you.

107
00:08:34,120 --> 00:08:37,159
She always does everything you tell her.

108
00:08:38,440 --> 00:08:39,720
This is not a big deal.

109
00:08:39,860 --> 00:08:42,299
Can’t you let her do what she wants for once?

110
00:08:46,090 --> 00:08:47,000
No.

111
00:08:48,870 --> 00:08:50,300
I can’t let it happen.

112
00:09:03,730 --> 00:09:06,400
My mom is the real last boss.

113
00:09:07,320 --> 00:09:08,560
She is worse than Jay.

114
00:09:08,940 --> 00:09:10,300
She is so self-centered.

115
00:09:10,800 --> 00:09:12,500
You need to be careful.

116
00:09:13,550 --> 00:09:15,480
I don’t know what she will do next.

117
00:09:16,200 --> 00:09:18,800
She has never backed down.

118
00:09:40,780 --> 00:09:42,370
So you met Mommy?

119
00:09:48,000 --> 00:09:49,000
Then…

120
00:09:50,160 --> 00:09:53,000
the fun has begun.

121
00:09:56,500 --> 00:09:58,100
Who did you call Mommy, Jay?

122
00:10:00,360 --> 00:10:04,600
Madam told me to call her Mommy.

123
00:10:06,280 --> 00:10:08,100
She is close to your aunt.

124
00:10:08,290 --> 00:10:09,960
She probably said that for the sake of their friendship.

125
00:10:10,000 --> 00:10:12,000
Stop thinking that you are important to her.

126
00:10:18,530 --> 00:10:19,400
Then…

127
00:10:21,150 --> 00:10:22,600
good luck.

128
00:10:57,240 --> 00:10:58,100
Hello.

129
00:11:26,550 --> 00:11:30,600
I think you should get to the point.

130
00:11:31,820 --> 00:11:33,350
What do you want to say to me?

131
00:11:39,340 --> 00:11:41,300
Are kids these days like you?

132
00:11:44,810 --> 00:11:45,900
No.

133
00:11:47,450 --> 00:11:50,600
Everyone is different.

134
00:11:52,780 --> 00:11:54,070
It’s just that…

135
00:11:55,650 --> 00:11:57,300
if we know that

136
00:11:58,930 --> 00:12:02,560
someone is trying to pick a fight with us or look down on us,

137
00:12:03,570 --> 00:12:05,300
kids these days won’t put up with it.

138
00:12:06,660 --> 00:12:07,600
You are disrespectful.

139
00:12:09,280 --> 00:12:13,180
But I don’t use violence with anyone.

140
00:12:15,110 --> 00:12:16,600
I fight back with reasons.

141
00:12:17,440 --> 00:12:18,600
Reasons?

142
00:12:19,550 --> 00:12:20,890
You are just talking back to me.

143
00:12:23,450 --> 00:12:25,770
It depends on whether you are willing to listen to me or not.

144
00:12:26,280 --> 00:12:27,450
If you are not,

145
00:12:28,100 --> 00:12:29,900
you will view it as me talking back to you.

146
00:12:32,100 --> 00:12:33,200
You know what?

147
00:12:33,480 --> 00:12:36,720
No kid has ever talked back to me like this.

148
00:12:38,340 --> 00:12:40,340
Jay grew up in Western culture.

149
00:12:40,380 --> 00:12:42,130
She’s always respectful to me.

150
00:12:42,170 --> 00:12:43,170
Unlike you.

151
00:12:46,740 --> 00:12:50,100
Has she seen you slap your daughter?

152
00:12:53,390 --> 00:12:54,760
If she saw it,

153
00:12:56,220 --> 00:12:57,900
she wouldn’t have been respectful to you.

154
00:13:04,880 --> 00:13:06,000
Now, I’m certain

155
00:13:08,540 --> 00:13:10,500
that you and I can't coexist.

156
00:13:14,030 --> 00:13:15,970
You are not good enough for my family.

157
00:13:17,860 --> 00:13:19,170
I think you should leave.

158
00:13:20,350 --> 00:13:22,040
There’s no point in trying to make it work.

159
00:13:22,080 --> 00:13:23,800
You two will end up breaking up anyway.

160
00:13:29,130 --> 00:13:33,200
I will never break up with Chan because someone tells me to do so.

161
00:13:35,100 --> 00:13:39,580
The only way I will leave her is if she asks me to.

162
00:13:44,730 --> 00:13:48,600
Do you think Chan will choose you?

163
00:13:50,650 --> 00:13:53,100
When it’s time for her to choose,

164
00:13:56,460 --> 00:13:57,900
do you think…

165
00:13:58,540 --> 00:14:00,200
you are good enough for Chan?

166
00:14:01,660 --> 00:14:03,400
Do you think

167
00:14:06,820 --> 00:14:08,700
you are different from your mom?

168
00:14:14,070 --> 00:14:16,500
All the scandals about your mom.

169
00:14:18,580 --> 00:14:20,900
Her uncontrollable temper.

170
00:14:23,670 --> 00:14:24,830
Your mom was ill.

171
00:14:24,870 --> 00:14:27,200
How can you be sure that you won’t have the same illness?

172
00:14:28,130 --> 00:14:31,600
You will damage Chan’s reputation.

173
00:14:32,060 --> 00:14:33,400
Just like your mom did.

174
00:14:42,160 --> 00:14:42,960
Key.

175
00:14:43,500 --> 00:14:44,300
Let’s go.

176
00:14:44,920 --> 00:14:45,650
Chan.

177
00:14:46,820 --> 00:14:48,400
You can’t do this to me.

178
00:14:48,820 --> 00:14:50,000
Are you crazy?

179
00:14:50,210 --> 00:14:51,200
Mom.

180
00:14:51,630 --> 00:14:52,900
I love you.

181
00:14:53,640 --> 00:14:54,750
But I’m asking you.

182
00:14:54,790 --> 00:14:57,400
Please stop saying hurtful things to the woman I love.

183
00:14:58,450 --> 00:14:59,500
If you won’t stop,

184
00:15:00,190 --> 00:15:01,800
I’ll have to protect my girl.

185
00:15:03,150 --> 00:15:04,550
Let’s go, Key.

186
00:15:09,120 --> 00:15:09,900
Chan.

187
00:15:23,150 --> 00:15:24,900
It’s good that Sun called to tell me about it.

188
00:15:25,380 --> 00:15:27,730
I couldn’t tell what would happen if I weren’t there.

189
00:15:33,670 --> 00:15:36,940
Even if you weren’t there, I could handle it.

190
00:15:38,380 --> 00:15:39,800
Why didn’t you tell me?

191
00:15:41,030 --> 00:15:44,900
If my mom does something like this again, you need to tell me right away.

192
00:15:45,050 --> 00:15:46,720
Don’t go to meet her alone.

193
00:16:01,840 --> 00:16:02,930
I like it

194
00:16:04,310 --> 00:16:05,800
when you are protecting me.

195
00:16:10,300 --> 00:16:11,600
I promise.

196
00:16:12,320 --> 00:16:14,380
I will never let anyone hurt you again.

197
00:16:17,720 --> 00:16:20,030
I’ll protect you for the rest of my life.

198
00:16:33,300 --> 00:16:38,100
Do you love me that much?

199
00:16:42,100 --> 00:16:43,100
Of course.

200
00:16:53,570 --> 00:16:54,770
Now, I feel a bit bad.

201
00:16:59,070 --> 00:17:00,400
Why did you say that?

202
00:17:05,359 --> 00:17:09,000
I just feel like…

203
00:17:11,170 --> 00:17:12,770
I’m causing you a problem,

204
00:17:15,720 --> 00:17:19,970
and I'm making you stressed about protecting me.

205
00:17:27,319 --> 00:17:28,450
Don’t worry about that.

206
00:17:30,830 --> 00:17:32,800
All I want is that you never let my hand go.

207
00:18:35,550 --> 00:18:36,700
Hello, Mommy.

208
00:18:37,090 --> 00:18:38,380
-Hello. -Have a seat.

209
00:18:40,460 --> 00:18:42,300
Madam wants to talk to you.

210
00:18:44,710 --> 00:18:45,730
What do you want to talk to me about?

211
00:18:46,380 --> 00:18:49,450
Aunt, you should have called me. So I would have hurried back home.

212
00:18:49,950 --> 00:18:51,300
It’s okay, Jay.

213
00:18:52,010 --> 00:18:53,400
I can wait for you.

214
00:18:58,200 --> 00:18:59,600
What do you want to talk about?

215
00:19:01,430 --> 00:19:02,900
She needs your help.

216
00:19:07,170 --> 00:19:08,380
Help with what?

217
00:19:10,400 --> 00:19:13,450
It’s something I’m sure you will be willing to help with.

218
00:19:15,570 --> 00:19:16,690
Is it about Chan?

219
00:19:18,250 --> 00:19:19,100
Yes.

220
00:19:21,760 --> 00:19:23,700
I don’t think Key…

221
00:19:24,620 --> 00:19:26,400
is a good match for my daughter.

222
00:19:27,950 --> 00:19:31,700
My daughter deserves someone better.

223
00:19:34,090 --> 00:19:34,900
Yes.

224
00:19:36,120 --> 00:19:37,500
I agree with you.

225
00:19:40,330 --> 00:19:41,850
What do you want me to do?

226
00:19:43,380 --> 00:19:47,370
You just get between them and break them up.

227
00:19:50,350 --> 00:19:51,700
I tried,

228
00:19:52,580 --> 00:19:53,600
but I failed.

229
00:19:57,810 --> 00:19:59,700
Are you going to give up?

230
00:20:04,100 --> 00:20:06,100
Chan is so into that girl.

231
00:20:07,180 --> 00:20:09,700
She doesn’t listen to anyone, not even me.

232
00:20:13,500 --> 00:20:15,370
She doesn’t listen to me either.

233
00:20:16,640 --> 00:20:18,400
I didn’t want to give up.

234
00:20:20,570 --> 00:20:22,100
But I know Chan well.

235
00:20:23,980 --> 00:20:25,100
Right now,

236
00:20:27,120 --> 00:20:28,800
she insists on being with Key.

237
00:20:30,760 --> 00:20:32,640
You two were in a relationship.

238
00:20:32,850 --> 00:20:35,120
I’m sure she still has some feelings for you.

239
00:20:35,430 --> 00:20:39,050
If you keep pursuing her, there will be a rift between them.

240
00:20:41,710 --> 00:20:45,000
You want me to cause a rift between them?

241
00:20:51,050 --> 00:20:52,970
Can I ask you something?

242
00:20:53,630 --> 00:20:54,470
Yes.

243
00:20:59,000 --> 00:21:00,100
What if…

244
00:21:02,610 --> 00:21:04,500
Chan broke up with Key,

245
00:21:06,610 --> 00:21:09,200
would you support my relationship with Chan?

246
00:21:12,450 --> 00:21:14,380
Of course.

247
00:21:18,430 --> 00:21:20,100
Would you support us getting married?

248
00:21:32,350 --> 00:21:33,350
I think…

249
00:21:33,790 --> 00:21:38,070
talking about marriage is a bit too far.

250
00:21:43,560 --> 00:21:44,600
I know that

251
00:21:45,240 --> 00:21:49,300
you will never support Chan in marrying a woman.

252
00:21:53,110 --> 00:21:55,050
Jay, you overthink it.

253
00:21:55,090 --> 00:21:56,890
She didn’t say that.

254
00:21:57,280 --> 00:21:58,400
I’m not stupid.

255
00:21:58,910 --> 00:21:59,930
I can tell.

256
00:22:04,290 --> 00:22:05,200
So…

257
00:22:06,160 --> 00:22:07,500
I refuse to help you.

258
00:22:12,380 --> 00:22:13,500
I won’t do it.

259
00:22:14,450 --> 00:22:15,300
Jay!

260
00:22:16,790 --> 00:22:17,900
I told you.

261
00:22:18,480 --> 00:22:21,800
I will never let anyone boss me around again.

262
00:22:25,330 --> 00:22:26,200
Mommy.

263
00:22:27,430 --> 00:22:28,540
I’m sorry.

264
00:22:31,680 --> 00:22:33,000
Excuse me.

265
00:22:44,070 --> 00:22:45,850
I’m so sorry, Madam.

266
00:22:46,260 --> 00:22:48,100
I’ll talk to her again.

267
00:22:49,080 --> 00:22:50,100
Thank you.

268
00:22:53,480 --> 00:22:55,600
I think I’ll need a backup plan.

269
00:22:58,730 --> 00:23:01,900
Actually, I have an idea.

270
00:23:13,640 --> 00:23:16,730
Do you think you are different from your mom?

271
00:23:17,150 --> 00:23:19,500
Her uncontrollable temper.

272
00:23:19,570 --> 00:23:20,960
(I told you to stop crying.)

273
00:23:21,000 --> 00:23:22,200
(Don’t you hear me?)

274
00:23:22,450 --> 00:23:24,600
(Stop crying. Don’t you hear me?)

275
00:23:25,880 --> 00:23:28,300
(I don’t want to hear you crying.)

276
00:23:28,790 --> 00:23:29,530
(Stop it right now.)

277
00:23:29,570 --> 00:23:31,180
-Key. -I'm sorry.

278
00:23:31,210 --> 00:23:32,440
(I don’t want to hear it.)

