It was your fault, Key. Everyone will die because of you.

561
00:46:30,670 --> 00:46:31,780
Mom hated me because of you.

562
00:46:31,820 --> 00:46:32,970
It was your fault, Key.

563
00:46:33,300 --> 00:46:35,130
-Why were you even born? -Mom hit me because of you.

564
00:46:35,170 --> 00:46:36,650
-It was your fault. -I was hurt because of you.

565
00:46:36,900 --> 00:46:37,600
Why were you even born?

566
00:46:37,620 --> 00:46:38,830
Mom hit me because of you.

567
00:46:38,870 --> 00:46:39,740
Why were you even born?

568
00:46:39,770 --> 00:46:42,400
-Everyone will die because of you. -Everyone will die because of you.

569
00:46:42,520 --> 00:46:44,000
Everyone will die because of you.

570
00:46:45,640 --> 00:46:46,500
Mom.

571
00:46:51,910 --> 00:46:53,100
It was your fault.

572
00:46:54,230 --> 00:46:55,180
It’s because you came back.

573
00:46:55,220 --> 00:46:56,450
Why did you come back? Get out.

574
00:46:57,630 --> 00:46:59,700
Mom, it’s not true.

575
00:46:59,790 --> 00:47:00,800
Key.

576
00:47:12,050 --> 00:47:12,900
Chan.

577
00:47:13,840 --> 00:47:14,900
It was your fault.

578
00:47:15,880 --> 00:47:17,100
It was your fault.

579
00:47:17,540 --> 00:47:19,090
Everyone will die because of you.

580
00:47:21,750 --> 00:47:23,300
Mom didn’t love me because of you.

581
00:47:23,670 --> 00:47:25,180
Mom hit me because of you.

582
00:47:25,520 --> 00:47:26,500
It was your fault.

583
00:47:26,730 --> 00:47:28,500
Everyone will die because of you, Key.

584
00:47:28,540 --> 00:47:30,400
It was your fault. It was your fault.

585
00:47:31,180 --> 00:47:32,510
I was wrong.

586
00:47:32,550 --> 00:47:35,050
Why did you come back? Tell me why you came back.

587
00:48:42,730 --> 00:48:43,900
I’m sorry.

588
00:48:47,040 --> 00:48:50,050
Chan, I’m sorry.

589
00:50:02,360 --> 00:50:10,850
WHY DID YOU TURN OFF YOUR PHONE?

590
00:50:25,600 --> 00:50:26,800
(Hello, sis.)

591
00:50:27,530 --> 00:50:28,350
Sun.

592
00:50:29,040 --> 00:50:30,550
Key disappeared.

593
00:50:30,710 --> 00:50:32,570
(Since when?)

594
00:50:32,610 --> 00:50:33,900
I’m not sure.

595
00:50:34,310 --> 00:50:35,700
I woke up and couldn’t find her.

596
00:50:36,170 --> 00:50:37,500
She turned off her phone.

597
00:50:37,880 --> 00:50:40,330
I sent her messages, but she didn’t read them.

598
00:50:41,400 --> 00:50:43,180
Key has never done this before.

599
00:50:44,520 --> 00:50:45,700
I’m so confused.

600
00:50:46,130 --> 00:50:47,530
I don’t know what’s going on.

601
00:50:47,570 --> 00:50:49,800
(Sis, calm down.)

602
00:50:50,110 --> 00:50:51,700
(Why don’t you talk to Peach?)

603
00:50:53,270 --> 00:50:54,000
Okay.

604
00:50:54,110 --> 00:50:57,100
I’ll call Peach.

605
00:50:57,820 --> 00:50:59,400
(Please keep me posted.)

606
00:50:59,770 --> 00:51:01,180
Okay, I will.

607
00:51:06,740 --> 00:51:08,150
Peach.

608
00:51:17,480 --> 00:51:18,600
Yes, Madam.

609
00:51:18,980 --> 00:51:21,580
You just keep pressuring her like this.

610
00:51:21,720 --> 00:51:23,200
Chan will give in one day.

611
00:51:23,560 --> 00:51:25,900
There’s been a lot of backlash.

612
00:51:26,000 --> 00:51:29,980
Key’s past behaviors are quite scandalous.

613
00:51:30,390 --> 00:51:32,100
She is the black sheep in her family.

614
00:51:32,480 --> 00:51:35,280
She is surely not good enough for Chan.

615
00:51:36,560 --> 00:51:37,300
Yes.

616
00:51:37,740 --> 00:51:39,430
If there’s anything else I can help you with,

617
00:51:39,470 --> 00:51:40,770
please let me know.

618
00:51:41,510 --> 00:51:43,200
Yes. Goodbye.

619
00:51:48,710 --> 00:51:49,800
You scared me.

620
00:51:50,720 --> 00:51:52,090
You showed up out of nowhere.

621
00:51:54,350 --> 00:51:55,800
What did you do?

622
00:51:57,700 --> 00:51:59,400
I’m just helping Madam Chanya.

623
00:51:59,880 --> 00:52:01,500
You refused to help her.

624
00:52:02,870 --> 00:52:05,090
Why are you getting involved in her business?

625
00:52:05,340 --> 00:52:08,410
Jay, what I’m doing will benefit us.

626
00:52:08,730 --> 00:52:12,000
If we help her now, she will help us in the future.

627
00:52:14,900 --> 00:52:16,400
Can you please stop doing this?

628
00:52:16,760 --> 00:52:17,700
Why?

629
00:52:17,910 --> 00:52:19,930
What I’m doing is good for you.

630
00:52:20,410 --> 00:52:22,780
You don’t like that girl either.

631
00:52:24,940 --> 00:52:27,400
But I’ll never ruin anyone’s life.

632
00:52:28,940 --> 00:52:31,610
If we don’t do this, you will lose.

633
00:52:32,780 --> 00:52:35,200
I don’t want to see you come home drunk every night.

634
00:52:35,240 --> 00:52:36,900
I’m worried about you. I don’t like it.

635
00:52:40,340 --> 00:52:41,800
I’m worried about you.

636
00:52:42,470 --> 00:52:44,000
I’m trying to help you, Jay.

637
00:52:47,230 --> 00:52:48,500
I love you.

638
00:52:50,670 --> 00:52:52,700
But can you leave me alone?

639
00:52:55,370 --> 00:52:56,570
I don’t need your help.

640
00:53:09,010 --> 00:53:11,400
Key used to have bad dreams when she was young.

641
00:53:12,590 --> 00:53:14,000
I thought it was gone.

642
00:53:16,420 --> 00:53:19,970
Every time she has this dream, she always runs away.

643
00:53:21,240 --> 00:53:24,300
Do you know what her dream is about?

644
00:53:25,180 --> 00:53:27,600
Why does she always disappear when she has the dream?

645
00:53:33,500 --> 00:53:35,400
After her mom died,

646
00:53:37,230 --> 00:53:38,900
she started to have nightmares.

647
00:53:40,020 --> 00:53:41,400
She saw herself in the dream.

648
00:53:42,710 --> 00:53:44,250
But it was not her.

649
00:53:46,140 --> 00:53:48,070
It was Key who was lonely

650
00:53:49,350 --> 00:53:50,600
and scary.

651
00:53:54,310 --> 00:53:55,750
Key told me

652
00:53:56,710 --> 00:54:01,100
it was the shadow that kept haunting her in her dream.

653
00:54:01,450 --> 00:54:05,090
It kept telling her to leave everyone.

654
00:54:05,350 --> 00:54:07,470
It blamed her that it was her fault

655
00:54:08,000 --> 00:54:09,400
and that she was bad luck.

656
00:54:09,440 --> 00:54:11,980
She was the reason why bad things happened…

657
00:54:13,640 --> 00:54:15,700
to her mom and everyone she loved.

658
00:54:21,300 --> 00:54:24,600
I feel really bad for her, Chan.

659
00:54:28,450 --> 00:54:29,980
Since her mom died,

660
00:54:30,950 --> 00:54:32,700
she kept blaming herself

661
00:54:33,630 --> 00:54:36,850
for being the reason why her mom decided to kill herself.

662
00:54:37,180 --> 00:54:39,200
It was not her fault.

663
00:54:39,590 --> 00:54:42,200
Pin had had mental problems for a long time.

664
00:54:42,450 --> 00:54:44,210
Her condition was getting worse

665
00:54:45,690 --> 00:54:47,500
when she was pregnant with Key.

666
00:54:49,070 --> 00:54:53,600
Pin believed that her life was ruined because she gave birth to Key.

667
00:54:58,150 --> 00:54:59,800
Aunt Pin was unstable.

668
00:55:00,740 --> 00:55:04,700
Sometimes, she hurt Key.

669
00:55:05,650 --> 00:55:07,300
She always told Key to get out of the house.

670
00:55:07,460 --> 00:55:12,100
Sometimes, she took Key out and left her.

671
00:55:12,350 --> 00:55:14,380
Key had to find her way home by herself.

672
00:55:15,070 --> 00:55:18,600
It was like she wanted Key to be away from her.

673
00:55:18,810 --> 00:55:20,700
So she wouldn’t hurt Key.

674
00:55:21,380 --> 00:55:24,500
Every time that Key found her way home,

675
00:55:25,280 --> 00:55:27,200
Aunt Pin’s condition would get worse.

676
00:55:28,490 --> 00:55:31,180
I tried to help Key’s mom get help from doctors.

677
00:55:32,060 --> 00:55:33,850
I guess I didn’t do a good job.

678
00:55:38,820 --> 00:55:41,800
It’s my fault that things turned out this way.

679
00:55:43,950 --> 00:55:45,700
I hurt this family.

680
00:55:58,020 --> 00:55:59,400
When I was in college,

681
00:56:00,640 --> 00:56:02,500
I met Key in the mountains.

682
00:56:05,330 --> 00:56:06,800
I went there to watch the stars.

683
00:56:08,020 --> 00:56:10,300
I found her walking alone in the forest.

684
00:56:12,570 --> 00:56:14,700
Hey, are you okay?

685
00:56:22,500 --> 00:56:26,500
You are the one who saved her back then?

686
00:56:32,140 --> 00:56:33,500
It’s such a small world.

687
00:56:34,940 --> 00:56:38,100
Maybe it’s their destiny.

688
00:56:41,520 --> 00:56:43,570
So Key was left in the forest

689
00:56:44,320 --> 00:56:46,100
by her mom?

690
00:56:47,580 --> 00:56:48,470
Yes.

691
00:56:49,850 --> 00:56:53,000
At the time, we were looking everywhere for her.

692
00:56:54,350 --> 00:56:55,550
But we couldn’t find her.

693
00:56:56,180 --> 00:56:59,100
Suddenly, she came home.

694
00:57:00,050 --> 00:57:02,500
She refused to tell us what happened.

695
00:57:09,510 --> 00:57:10,370
(Chan.)

696
00:57:12,150 --> 00:57:13,100
(What?)

697
00:57:13,770 --> 00:57:14,950
I…

698
00:57:17,230 --> 00:57:18,700
When I’m older,

699
00:57:20,690 --> 00:57:22,340
I’ll get a moon tattoo…

700
00:57:25,860 --> 00:57:27,150
here.

701
00:57:30,400 --> 00:57:31,850
(You still haven’t told me)

702
00:57:34,450 --> 00:57:36,250
why you got the moon tattoo.

703
00:57:43,010 --> 00:57:44,500
Maybe one day,

704
00:57:47,430 --> 00:57:49,300
our paths may cross again.

705
00:57:55,530 --> 00:57:57,100
This will help you remember me.

706
00:58:06,890 --> 00:58:10,800
After she got home that day, she was blaming herself.

707
00:58:13,410 --> 00:58:14,380
Why?

708
00:58:19,550 --> 00:58:20,800
Not long after that,

709
00:58:21,530 --> 00:58:23,700
Aunt Pin decided to end her life.

710
00:58:25,820 --> 00:58:27,700
Key was the first one who found her body.

711
00:58:29,450 --> 00:58:32,900
After that night, she was haunted by the picture.

712
00:58:33,980 --> 00:58:35,750
She kept having bad dreams about it.

713
00:58:36,840 --> 00:58:38,960
She’d seen a psychiatrist for a long time

714
00:58:39,530 --> 00:58:41,240
before she got better.

715
00:58:41,870 --> 00:58:43,050
Even so,

716
00:58:43,890 --> 00:58:46,400
she decided to move out and live on her own.

717
00:58:58,830 --> 00:59:01,820
She probably doesn’t want to live in the house

718
00:59:01,860 --> 00:59:03,900
that reminds her of the incident.

719
00:59:05,370 --> 00:59:06,850
All we can do is wait.

720
00:59:08,430 --> 00:59:11,400
We pray that she will be ready to come home one day.

721
00:59:12,930 --> 00:59:16,400
I thought that she was fully recovered.

722
00:59:30,940 --> 00:59:32,850
Is there anything we can do to help Key?

723
00:59:34,690 --> 00:59:38,100
Do you know where she might be?

724
00:59:51,660 --> 00:59:54,600
She ran away from home several times.

725
00:59:55,510 --> 00:59:58,100
She didn’t contact us at all.

726
00:59:59,080 --> 01:00:00,500
When she felt better,

727
01:00:01,370 --> 01:00:02,920
she would come back.

728
01:00:04,230 --> 01:00:06,300
We should go and look for her.

729
01:00:09,400 --> 01:00:10,200
Yes.

730
01:00:10,630 --> 01:00:11,900
I’ll help you.

731
01:01:06,130 --> 01:01:07,430
(Where are you, Key?)

732
01:01:17,140 --> 01:01:18,400
(I’ll find you.)

733
01:01:36,760 --> 01:01:37,650
Hello, Key.

734
01:01:37,920 --> 01:01:39,580
(Where are you? Are you okay?)

735
01:01:39,630 --> 01:01:41,100
Can you not tell Chan about this?

736
01:01:41,370 --> 01:01:44,890
I don’t want her to see me like this.

737
01:01:44,920 --> 01:01:46,210
Cancel today’s meeting.

738
01:01:46,300 --> 01:01:47,170
Where are you going?

739
01:01:47,510 --> 01:01:48,450
I’m going to find Key.

740
01:01:48,730 --> 01:01:50,240
How dare you show up here?

741
01:01:50,350 --> 01:01:54,450
Do you know that your mom asked me to steal Chan from Key?

742
01:01:54,650 --> 01:01:55,700
But I refused to do it.

743
01:01:56,200 --> 01:01:57,200
Liar.

744
01:01:57,930 --> 01:02:00,400
You spent ten years looking for me.

745
01:02:00,990 --> 01:02:04,930
I’ll find you even though I don’t know where you are.

746
01:02:05,330 --> 01:02:06,770
I will take you home.
